---

## Edge Cases

| Scenario | Handling |
|----------|----------|
| No git changes | Do nothing, notify user |
| Merge conflicts present | Notify user and STOP |
| No remote configured | Ask user for remote URL |
| README.md has no URL | Ask user for project URL |
| Vercel deploy takes too long | Notify user and ask how to proceed |
| Site completely down (500 errors) | Ask user and STOP |
| Conflicting user instructions | Ask for clarification |
| Massive diff (50+ files) | Filter to meaningful changes; user may provide clues via params |
| Binary files in diff | Include in commit; user provides context |
| User tries to run twice simultaneously | Block and refuse; never allow concurrent runs |

---

## Important Rules

- **Commit messages must be specific.** "feat: add button" is not acceptable. "feat: add 'Save Draft' button to post editor" is.
- **Always test new features first**, then regression test existing functionality.
- **Reports must be detailed.** "Everything works" is not acceptable. Specific observations are required.
- **Capture end-user feelings** (confusion, delight, friction) not just technical facts.
- **Think like a senior engineer** — spot hidden bugs and cleaner implementations.
- **Proactive communication** — tell user what you're doing during waits.
- **Respect user overrides** — if user says "keep reports folder", keep it.
- **Never run concurrently** — block second requests if one is running.
